  {
   "id": "VY_yW1AX534J",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2015-06-17T15:21:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: mirt simdata Error in sample.int(length(x), size, replace, prob): too few positive probabilities",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Daniel,<div><br></div><div>It looks like you may be using a version of mirt that is out of date (the error I got first was that the &#39;itemtype&#39; argument was missing). So I would recommend updating (version 1.10 is the latest) and trying the following code instead:</div><div><br></div><div>```</div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>library(mirt)</div><div>a &lt;- matrix(c(1.5, NA, 0.5, NA, 1, NA, 1, 0.5, NA, 1.5, NA, 0.5,</div><div>              NA, 1, NA, 1), ncol = 2, byrow = TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>d &lt;- matrix(c(-1, NA, NA, -1.5, NA, NA, 1.5, NA, NA, 0, NA, NA,</div><div>              3, 2, -0.5, 2.5, 1, -1, 2, 0, NA, 1, NA, NA), </div><div>            ncol = 3, byrow = TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>sigma &lt;- diag(2)</div><div>sigma[1, 2] &lt;- sigma[2, 1] &lt;- 0.4</div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>itemtype &lt;- rep(&#39;dich&#39;, 8)</div><div>itemtype[5:7] &lt;- &#39;graded&#39;</div><div>simdata2 &lt;- simdata(a, d, 2000, sigma, itemtype = itemtype)</div></div><div>```</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers.</div><div><br></div><div>Phil</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jun 17, 2015 at 11:08 AM, Daniel Anderson <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dan...@uoregon.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
