     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:19px\">Hi all,</span><br><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19px\">I&#39;m trying to understand the  <code style=\"font-size:13px;padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);white-space:pre-wrap\">simdata()</code> function, as I&#39;d eventually like to use it to simulate responses from a multidimensional item response model for a paper I&#39;m working on. Unfortunately, I keep running into the error noted in the title.<br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19px\">In the <a href=\"http://www.jstatsoft.org/v48/i06/paper\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jstatsoft.org/v48/i06/paper&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475594124000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06Lz8gGqhwd51E7Y2Syl7T\">jstat article introducing the package</a>, simulated data are used to illustrate the <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);white-space:pre-wrap\">confmirt()</code>function, and the code used to produce the simulated data is presented in Appendix B, as</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;overflow:aut