   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Perfect, thanks so much! I believe my error, actually, was in assuming that all items were dichotomous, without looking at the d matrix close enough. In the text below the code block you can see where I was trying to re-specify the simulation while (incorrectly) declaring the item types. <div><br></div><div>Thanks so much for your help, it is much appreciated.<div><br></div><div>Daniel</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br><br>On Wednesday, June 17, 2015 at 8:21:47 AM UTC-7, Phil Chalmers wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Daniel,<div><br></div><div>It looks like you may be using a version of mirt that is out of date (the error I got first was that the &#39;itemtype&#39; argument was missing). So I would recommend updating (version 1.10 is the latest) and trying the following code instead:</div><div><br></div><div>```</div><div><div>library(mirt)</div><div>a &lt;- matrix(c(1.5, NA, 0.5, NA, 1, NA, 1, 0.5, NA, 1.5, NA, 0.5,</div><div>              NA, 1, NA, 1), ncol = 2, byrow = TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>d &lt;- matrix(c(-1, NA, NA, -1.5, NA, NA, 1.5, NA, NA, 0, NA, NA,</div><div>              3, 2, -0.5, 2.5, 1, -1, 2, 0, NA, 1, NA, NA), </div><div>            ncol = 3, byrow = TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>sigma &lt;- diag(2)</div><div>sigma[1, 2] &lt;- sigma[2, 1] &lt;- 0.4</div><div><br></div><div>itemtype &lt;- rep(&#39;dich&#39;, 8)</div><div>itemtype[5:7] &lt;- &#39;graded&#39;</div><div>simdata2 &lt;- simdata(a, d, 2000, sigma, itemtype = itemtype)</div></div><div>```</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers.</div><div><br></div><div>Phil</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jun 17, 2015 at 11:08 AM, Daniel Anderson <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">dan...@uoregon.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:19px\">Hi all,</span><br><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19px\">I&#39;m trying to understand the  <code style=\"font-size:13px;padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);white-space:pre-wrap\">simdata()</code> function, as I&#39;d eventually like to use it to simulate responses from a multidimensional item response model for a paper I&#39;m working on. Unfortunately, I keep running into the error noted in the title.<br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19px\">In the <a href=\"http://www.jstatsoft.org/v48/i06/paper\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jstatsoft.org/v48/i06/paper&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475594138000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1rktUmh9q_eRlFuQ4bT0sh\">jstat article introducing the package</a>, simulated data are used to illustrate the <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);white-space:pre-wrap\">confmirt()</code>function, and the code used to produce the simulated data is presented in Appendix B, as</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;overflow:auto;width:auto;max-height:600px;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">library</